{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c52f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075ff-68a1-7c53-bd42-f28c0c61d002"},"sequence":242,"recorded_at":1780531400000479,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"9f6f96de-19b7-4e55-8d18-de7846fe095d"},"task_id":"9f6f96de-19b7-4e55-8d18-de7846fe095d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"9f6f96de-19b7-4e55-8d18-de7846fe095d","chunk":"Read text file `internal/dirnode/arm_reachability_test.go`.\n1|package dirnode\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"go/ast\"\n5|\t\"os\"\n6|\t\"sort\"\n7|\t\"strings\"\n8|\t\"testing\"\n9|\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n11|)\n12|\n13|// This file is the derived arm-reachability gate (review round 3,\n14|// C1). The arm census in census_test.go derives every refusal arm\n15|// from production source and maps each to witness tests, but it\n16|// never checks that a witness actually fires the arm it names: a\n17|// vector carrying two defects is satisfied by whichever arm fires\n18|// first, and three committed \"unknown member\" vectors proved this\n19|// by reaching a strict-decode, operation, and node-build arm while\n20|// naming the envelope unknown-member arm. A code-only assertion\n21|// cannot tell those paths apart, and a deleted-member vector\n22|// refuses downstream with the same code, so code-only witnesses\n23|// leave missing-member, extensions, and empty-frame arms deletable\n24|// with a green suite.\n25|//\n26|// The gate below closes the class without another hand audit.\n27|// Every row pairs one production-derived arm key with a vector\n28|// driven through a production entry, and the test computes which\n29|// arm the vector actually reaches from the refusal message:\n30|//\n31|//   - a literal arm (ctor|<ctor>|<detail>) matches when the message\n32|//     carries its full detail; the row passes only when exactly the\n33|//     named literal matches, so a vector that slides to a sibling\n34|//     arm or to the strict conduit fails naming the arm it reached;\n35|//   - a fault conduit (...\"<prefix> \"+fault.detail) or a\n36|//     context-prefixed arm (context+\"<suffix>\") matches on its\n37|//     derived prefix/suffix; the row passes only when the named arm\n38|//     matches, no literal matches, and every other match is at most\n39|//     one frame fault travelling the same conduit;\n40|//   - a frame fault (frame|<detail>) matches on its detail and pins\n41|//     its carrier conduit through the also key, so the fault and\n42|//     the entry that carried it are both derived.\n43|//\n44|// A row whose reached arm cannot be determined — no match, or a\n45|// match set outside the shapes above — fails, never passes. The\n46|// roster fails closed in both directions: an arm with no row fails\n47|// unless it carries a defensive rationale in defensiveArms, and a\n48|// row naming an arm production no longer derives fails as\n49|// orphaned. Expected messages are never retyped here: they come\n50|// from the derived keys, so a reworded production arm fails its\n51|// row instead of passing against a stale copy.\n52|//\n53|// The checkResponseIdentity context arms instantiate with the call\n54|// site's context word. TestReachabilityContextsAreClosed derives\n55|// the context set from production calls and requires exactly\n56|// success and failure, so the matcher below cannot silently miss a\n57|// third instantiation.\n58|\n59|// armReachRow pairs one derived arm key with the vector that fires\n60|// it. also optionally names a second derived key whose text must\n61|// also match: frame-fault rows pin the carrier conduit that way.\n62|type armReachRow struct {\n63|\tarm   string\n64|\tname  string\n65|\tdrive func(t *testing.T) error\n66|\talso  string\n67|}\n68|\n69|// rowName renders the subtest name for one row: the arm key,\n70|// entry-suffixed for the one key emitted at two production sites.\n71|func (row armReachRow) rowName() string {\n72|\tif row.name != \"\" {\n73|\t\treturn row.name\n74|\t}\n75|\treturn row.arm\n76|}\n77|\n78|// deriveLiteralArmSiteCounts counts production call sites per\n79|// literal arm key. Most literals are emitted once; a literal\n80|// emitted at two sites shares one arm key, and the roster below\n81|// requires one firing vector per emitting site — a row driving\n82|// the other site cannot redden when this one is removed.\n83|func deriveLiteralArmSiteCounts(t *testing.T) map[string]int {\n84|\tt.Helper()\n85|\tregistered := map[string]bool{}\n86|\tfor _, name := range refusalConstructors {\n87|\t\tregistered[name] = true\n88|\t}\n89|\tcounts := map[string]int{}\n90|\tfor _, path := range productionFiles(t) {\n91|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n92|\t\tif err != nil {\n93|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"site counts: %v\", err)\n94|\t\t}\n95|\t\tsyntax, err := parseGoFile(path, source)\n96|\t\tif err != nil {\n97|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"site counts: %v\", err)\n98|\t\t}\n99|\t\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n100|\t\t\tfunction, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n101|\t\t\tif !ok || function.Body == nil {\n102|\t\t\t\treturn true\n103|\t\t\t}\n104|\t\t\tast.Inspect(function.Body, func(inner ast.Node) bool {\n105|\t\t\t\tcall, ok := inner.(*ast.CallExpr)\n106|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n107|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n108|\t\t\t\t}\n109|\t\t\t\ttarget, ok := call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)\n110|\t\t\t\tif !ok || !registered[target.Name] || len(call.Args) == 0 {\n111|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n112|\t\t\t\t}\n113|\t\t\t\tliteral, ok := call.Args[0].(*ast.BasicLit)\n114|\t\t\t\tif !ok {\n115|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n116|\t\t\t\t}\n117|\t\t\t\tcounts[target.Name+\"|\"+strings.Trim(literal.Value, `\"`)]++\n118|\t\t\t\treturn true\n119|\t\t\t})\n120|\t\t\treturn false\n(more lines below)"}}}
