{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c589","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075ff-68a1-7c53-bd42-f28c0c61d002"},"sequence":287,"recorded_at":1780531400000569,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"ab8aaf3e-2d06-4b3e-806b-4e349397f336"},"task_id":"ab8aaf3e-2d06-4b3e-806b-4e349397f336","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"ab8aaf3e-2d06-4b3e-806b-4e349397f336","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/protocol.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// Wire constants of pinned specification Section 7.8. The protocol\n12|// identifier and version are exact: the adapter speaks 1.0.0 in the\n13|// same trusted executable as Provider Protocol 2.0.0, and anything\n14|// else on the wire is a session_adapter_protocol_error, never a\n15|// negotiation.\n16|const (\n17|\t// ProtocolID is the exact protocol member every request and\n18|\t// response envelope carries.\n19|\tProtocolID = \"urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter\"\n20|\t// ProtocolVersion is the exact protocol_version member this host\n21|\t// writes and the only one it accepts a response under.\n22|\tProtocolVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n23|\t// ProtocolMajor is the major this host implements. Section 7.8\n24|\t// defines no multi-major negotiation for the adapter, so a\n25|\t// different major is an invalid envelope, not a downgrade.\n26|\tProtocolMajor = 1\n27|\t// ErrorVersion is the Structured Error version every failure\n28|\t// envelope carries: Session Adapter 1.0 statically binds\n29|\t// Structured Error 1.1.0.\n30|\tErrorVersion = axerror.Version110\n31|\t// MaxFrameBytes bounds one JSONL line in either direction:\n32|\t// Section 7.8 inherits Section 7.2's rule that every line is one\n33|\t// complete UTF-8 JSON object no larger than 8 MiB.\n34|\tMaxFrameBytes = 8 << 20\n35|)\n36|\n37|// Operation names one Section 7.8 registry entry. The registry is\n38|// closed: dispatch refuses any other name locally, before any adapter\n39|// surface is touched.\n40|type Operation string\n41|\n42|// Section 7.8 operation registry in the section's table order. The\n43|// inventory test derives this list from the pinned specification\n44|// text and requires exact ordered equality, so a dropped, added, or\n45|// reordered entry reddens there rather than passing silently.\n46|const (\n47|\tOpManifest       Operation = \"manifest\"\n48|\tOpProbe          Operation = \"probe\"\n49|\tOpDiscover       Operation = \"discover\"\n50|\tOpInspect        Operation = \"inspect\"\n51|\tOpSnapshotProof  Operation = \"snapshot-proof\"\n52|\tOpCapturePlan    Operation = \"capture-plan\"\n53|\tOpCapture        Operation = \"capture\"\n54|\tOpNormalize      Operation = \"normalize\"\n55|\tOpProjectionPlan Operation = \"projection-plan\"\n56|\tOpProject        Operation = \"project\"\n57|\tOpReadBack       Operation = \"read-back\"\n58|\tOpValidate       Operation = \"validate\"\n59|\tOpResumePlan     Operation = \"resume-plan\"\n60|\tOpDoctor         Operation = \"doctor\"\n61|)\n62|\n63|// operationOrder is the single construction site of the dispatch\n64|// registry.\n65|var operationOrder = []Operation{\n66|\tOpManifest,\n67|\tOpProbe,\n68|\tOpDiscover,\n69|\tOpInspect,\n70|\tOpSnapshotProof,\n71|\tOpCapturePlan,\n72|\tOpCapture,\n73|\tOpNormalize,\n74|\tOpProjectionPlan,\n75|\tOpProject,\n76|\tOpReadBack,\n77|\tOpValidate,\n78|\tOpResumePlan,\n79|\tOpDoctor,\n80|}\n(more lines below)"}}}
