live PIDs,\\n443:2. <a id=\\\"dir-inv-02\\\"></a><code>DIR-INV-02</code>: a cross-environment clone\\n535:33. <a id=\\\"dir-inv-33\\\"></a><code>DIR-INV-33</code>: cross-environment capture,\\n541:35. <a id=\\\"dir-inv-35\\\"></a><code>DIR-INV-35</code>: cross-environment move is\\n570:    argv, explicit working directory, and an environment allowlist; no\\n704:- <strong>Directory Node façade</strong>: exposes source-local environment\\n731:Every path class has one exact command flag and environment override. Path\\n733:corresponding non-empty environment override, then the platform default. A\\n744:This five-row table is the complete environment-override registry for version\\n746:<code>AX_</code> is ordinary process environment and MUST NOT be interpreted by\\n1281:| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\\n1491:| <code>env_literals</code> | map(environment-name,string)[0..64] | Non-secret literals of at most 4,096 UTF-8 bytes each; keys sorted in canonical form and disjoint from <code>env_names</code> |\\n1622:Session Record 2.0.0 is emitted in v0.3.0 only for a cross-environment clone\\n1630:<code>same_provider_fork</code>, and <code>cross_environment_clone</code>.\\n1632:protocol adopts them. Cross-environment clone contains exactly:\\n1634:- <code>kind=cross_environment_clone</code>, operation UUIDv7, and bundle UUIDv7;\\n1656:The <code>cross_environment_clone</code> variant's exact typed members are\\n1665:<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\\n1666:<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\\n1688:<code>cross_environment_clone</code>, and <code>native_adoption</code>. The\\n1695:<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\\n1703:immutable after creation. Cross-environment move uses the existing\\n1704:<code>cross_environment_clone</code> creation variant plus later Session Event\\n2097:NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\\n2345:be accepted in config fields; a provider MAY name a machine-local environment\\n2348:The complete 1.0.0 environment-override registry is\\n2541:<code>installation_id:digest</code>, <code>environment_id:string[1..64]</code>,\\n2556:<code>environment_observations</code>, <code>native_observations</code>,\\n2563:arbitrary environment passthrough. Model credentials resolve through a\\n2597:unrestricted environment, or environment passthrough is forbidden.\\n2611:credentials, auth databases, raw evidence secrets, environment values, or live\\n2742:<code>provider_timeout</code>. It MUST redact environment and stderr before\\n2890:| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\\n3110:secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\\n3489:Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\\n3517:| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4185,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1047,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
