ven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\\n1938:The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\\n1948:The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\\n3064:is no second tuple- or path-based idempotency key in provider protocol 2.0.0.\\n3111:advertised portable-store tuple and MUST separate durable includes,\\n3124:destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\\n3583:| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\\n3595:| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\\\|revoked\\\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\\n3668:accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\\n3718:response-plus-exit tuple authorizes the caller to launch a fresh process for\\n3727:failure, or any error other than the exact downgrade tuple is terminal and\\n3730:If every locally supported major returns the exact downgrade tuple, the caller\\n3760:<code>environment_tuple_registry_id:digest</code>,\\n3765:façade executable/module bindings and tuple declarations MUST agree; a\\n3831:Discovery may degrade for an unknown source tuple only when stable identity and\\n3853:  succeeds for the exact version/platform tuple;\\n3930:| Future plugin / any | ? / ? / ? | Disabled until a tuple-specific probe and acceptance record exist. |\\n6626:<code>environment_tuple:Envir