{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c871","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075ff-68a1-7c53-bd42-f28c0c61d002"},"sequence":659,"recorded_at":1780531400001313,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"025bfbeb-85db-485b-b12b-bded340ca2ab"},"task_id":"025bfbeb-85db-485b-b12b-bded340ca2ab","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"025bfbeb-85db-485b-b12b-bded340ca2ab","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessadapter implements the ax host side of the companion\n2|// Session Adapter protocol of pinned specification Section 7.8: the\n3|// closed operation registry, envelope framing, manifest and probe\n4|// validation, call-context and authority gates, resource limits,\n5|// request-digest binding, discovery binding, and Environment Tuple\n6|// admission.\n7|//\n8|// The actor every Section 7.8 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax\n9|// host (this repository). The session adapter is a child surface this\n10|// package never trusts: it runs in the same trusted\n11|// ax-provider-<id> executable as Provider Protocol 2.0.0 and is not a\n12|// separately discovered plugin, so discovery here means binding the\n13|// adapter to the independently observed provider candidate — the same\n14|// executable path, the same host-observed executable digest, the same\n15|// provider identifier, and the same manifest digest — before every\n16|// call and every target mutation. Every byte the adapter emits is\n17|// attacker-influenced, so every frame is validated before any member\n18|// is used.\n19|//\n20|// This package owns the closed-object decoders and the fail-closed\n21|// gates. Operation dispatch means the host maps an operation name to\n22|// one adapter invocation and refuses unknown names locally with\n23|// operation_unknown; an unavailable operation is refused with\n24|// capability_unavailable. A failed read is never an absence: a\n25|// partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped result is a\n26|// session_adapter_protocol_error, never an empty result and never\n27|// fallback permission.\n28|//\n29|// The package mutates no durable state of its own and keeps no\n30|// cross-call cache: adapter mutations address fresh isolated sinks\n31|// the core creates per call, and candidate objects are addressed only\n32|// by their exact *_candidate_id in the request's sink. The core\n33|// retrieves, validates, rehashes, and seals them. Retry receipts live\n34|// in the core and the sink, not in the host: Section 7.8 defines no\n35|// (operation, operation_id) retry key — the pinned catalog carries an\n36|// empty mutation-group list for the session_adapter family — so the\n37|// idempotency this package enforces is the request-digest binding\n38|// (the adapter answers for exactly the canonical body the host sent)\n39|// and the byte-for-byte context echo, plus the fresh-sink authority\n40|// rule that keeps one call's writes out of every other call's sink.\n41|// Cross-crash durability of adapter results is the core document's\n42|// property, the same division the provider host records for its\n43|// transaction document.\n44|//\n45|// Stated bounds: transport process management (spawning the provider\n46|// executable, deadlines, stdio ownership) belongs to the caller, which\n47|// supplies frames this package validates as bytes; nested objects\n48|// owned by Sections 13.14 and 10.8 (CaptureBoundary, NativeIdentity,\n49|// StableSnapshotProof, CloneSourceSummary, FidelityCounts,\n50|// WorkspaceBinding, and the remaining clone-plan types) are checked\n51|// for presence and object shape only, never for content — their\n52|// content owners are the directory-node and boundary leaves of this\n53|// Story, and inventing their validation here would collide with that\n54|// ownership at integration. The tuple-registry signature, sequence\n55|// monotonicity, and publication rules of Section 13.14 fail closed at\n56|// the registry owner, which does not exist yet; this package admits\n57|// single entries against caller-held registry facts. Resume-smoke\n58|// family and secret checks on resume-plan argv rest on\n59|// ResumeSmokeEvidence (native_cli_family), which lives in the same\n60|// unowned registry scope: this package enforces the exact-once\n61|// identity occurrence and the argv shape, not the family name or the\n62|// absence of secrets.\n63|package sessadapter"}}}
