{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c875","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a075ff-68a1-7c53-bd42-f28c0c61d002"},"sequence":661,"recorded_at":1780531400001317,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01319f54-880e-4865-b5c8-fc6dd7d16451"},"call_id":"call_01a07600db2e77328ff95481eed17542","text":"Read text file `internal/dirnode/doc.go`.\n1|// Package dirnode implements the ax host side of the companion\n2|// Directory Node protocol of pinned specification Section 7.9: the\n3|// two-major bootstrap, envelope framing, manifest and probe\n4|// validation, scan/inventory request framing with (operation,\n5|// operation_id) idempotency, Session Directory Query framing of\n6|// Section 10.8.5, façade binding checks, and Structured Error\n7|// 1.2.0 refusals.\n8|//\n9|// The actor every Section 7.9 RFC 2119 keyword governs here is the ax\n10|// host (this repository). The directory node is a child surface this\n11|// package never trusts: it runs in the same per-environment\n12|// implementation as Provider 2 and Session Adapter 1, and every byte\n13|// it emits is attacker-influenced, so every frame is validated\n14|// before any member is used. Neither major adds operations to\n15|// Provider 2, executes Continuation Plans, or transports\n16|// transcript/workspace bytes, and this host never asks for any of\n17|// those through this package.\n18|//\n19|// Major negotiation is caller-driven enumeration, not a hello: the\n20|// caller attempts its locally supported majors in strictly\n21|// descending order with one manifest request each, each attempt on a\n22|// fresh process. Only the exact downgrade tuple — one well-framed\n23|// failure echoing the request, response schema_version 1.0.0,\n24|// Structured Error 1.2 incompatible_protocol with exit 6 and\n25|// retryable=false, then process exit 6 — authorizes the next lower\n26|// attempt. Deciding that tuple is DecideBootstrapStep; launching and\n27|// reaping processes belongs to the caller, which records each\n28|// attempt's process token in a ProcessGuard so a returned or failed\n29|// process is never reused for a lower major.\n30|//\n31|// A failed read is never an absence: a partial, malformed,\n32|// over-limit, mislabeled, or escaped result is an\n33|// adapter_protocol_violation or transport_failure, never an empty\n34|// result and never fallback permission. A syntactically valid frame\n35|// naming an unknown operation is operation_unknown, refused\n36|// locally before any node surface is touched. Query framing\n37|// defects are query_invalid.\n38|//\n39|// Stated bounds: transport process management (spawning the node\n40|// executable, deadlines, stdio ownership, allowlist/SSH admission)\n41|// belongs to the caller, which supplies frames this package\n42|// validates as bytes; the content of nested observation and lineage\n43|// types owned by Sections 10.8 and 13.14 (EnvironmentObservation,\n44|// NativeSessionObservation, InventoryBatch, PreviewExcerpt payload\n45|// meaning, EnrichmentJobRequest/Receipt chains, ManagementBinding\n46|// content, RuntimeExpectation) is checked for presence and object\n47|// shape only — the shared-environment leaf of this Story owns that\n48|// content, and inventing its validation here would collide with that\n49|// ownership at integration. The scan journal in this package is an\n50|// in-memory (operation, operation_id) record with byte export and\n51|// import so crash recovery is demonstrable; its durable placement is\n52|// the core's property. Caller authentication (CallerContext is\n53|// authenticated server-side, never accepted from an unverified body\n54|// alone) belongs to the caller: this package validates the context\n55|// shape. Section 10.8.5 prose names a query_cursor_mismatch code the\n56|// pinned error registry does not register; cursor reuse after a\n57|// bound change is refused here as query_invalid with a\n58|// cursor-mismatch detail, and the divergence is recorded on the\n59|// refusing call site, not hidden.\n60|package dirnode","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
